AWS & DevOps Tools Used in Project
🔹 Introduction

In this project, we use AWS and DevOps tools to build, deploy, and manage the application efficiently. These tools help in automation, scalability, and reliability.

☁️ AWS Services (What we will use in AWS)
1️⃣ EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)

👉 Used to create virtual servers
👉 Runs backend and deployment setup

2️⃣ ECR (Elastic Container Registry)

👉 Used to store Docker images
👉 Provides secure image management

3️⃣ EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service)

👉 Used to create and manage Kubernetes clusters
👉 Deploys the application in containerized form

4️⃣ RDS (Relational Database Service)

👉 Used to host MySQL database
👉 Stores application data securely

5️⃣ S3 (Simple Storage Service)

👉 Used to store static files like images, videos, and documents

6️⃣ IAM (Identity and Access Management)

👉 Used to manage users and roles
👉 Provides secure access control

7️⃣ Load Balancer (ELB)

👉 Distributes traffic across services
👉 Ensures high availability

8️⃣ CloudWatch (optional)

👉 Used for monitoring and logging

⚙️ DevOps Tools
1️⃣ Docker

👉 Used to containerize the application

2️⃣ Kubernetes

👉 Used to manage and scale containers

3️⃣ Jenkins / GitHub Actions

👉 Used for CI/CD pipeline

4️⃣ ArgoCD

👉 Used for continuous deployment

5️⃣ Terraform

👉 Used for Infrastructure as Code (automating AWS resources)

6️⃣ SonarQube

👉 Used for code quality analysis

🔄 CI/CD Flow
Code Push → Build → Docker Image → Push to ECR → Deploy to EKS → Access via Ingress
🎯 Conclusion

In this project, AWS and DevOps tools are used to create a scalable, secure, and automated system. This approach makes deployment faster and more efficient.
